101:3. **Fix synchronous IO. It can't be deferred.** Calls like `new Date()`, `Date.now()`, `Math.random()`, and `crypto.randomUUID()` during prerender throw a build error that `instant = false` does not clear, so a route that uses them won't build until you address it, opt-out or not. Move the call out of the prerendered shell so it runs at request time: wrap the part that needs it in [`<Suspense>`](https://react.dev/reference/react/Suspense) and call [`connection()`](/docs/app/api-reference/functions/connection) before the call, or move it into a Client Component.
